[E0350] Error: an owned closure cannot capture `values`, a reference
   ╭─[ err/201_futures/main.wip:9:37 ]
   │
 9 │     val sum = Future::run(own () => values.len())
   │                                     ───┬──  
   │                                        ╰──── captured here
   │ 
   │ Help: pass it to the closure as a parameter, or capture what it refers to by value
   │ 
   │ Note: an owned closure outlives the call that made it, and a reference does not
───╯
[E0427] Error: an `own` closure cannot hold a `str`
    ╭─[ err/201_futures/main.wip:15:39 ]
    │
 15 │     val count = Future::run(own () => piece.len())
    │                                       ──┬──  
    │                                         ╰──── a `str` borrows bytes that live somewhere else
    │ 
    │ Help: `String` owns its bytes, and hands out a `str` with `toStr()`
    │ 
    │ Note: a `str`, a `&` reference, a `view struct` and what holds one borrow what lives somewhere else, so they stand in a parameter, a local, a result and a view's field, and not where they would outlive it
────╯
[E0427] Error: an `own` closure cannot hold `Sender<str>`
    ╭─[ err/201_futures/main.wip:20:41 ]
    │
 20 │     val speaker = Future::run(own () => words.send("hi"))
    │                                         ──┬──  
    │                                           ╰──── `Sender<str>` borrows, as a `str` does
    │ 
    │ Help: `String` owns its bytes, and hands out a `str` with `toStr()`
    │ 
    │ Note: a `str`, a `&` reference, a `view struct` and what holds one borrow what lives somewhere else, so they stand in a parameter, a local, a result and a view's field, and not where they would outlive it
────╯
[E0420] Error: the compiler has no body for `intoAddress`
